<Root>
  <DefaultMacro>
    <Major></Major>
    <Description>The Super Jump macro in Combat Warriors is a powerful tool that allows players to execute high and far-reaching jumps, providing tactical advantages in combat and traversal. This macro combines precise timing and key inputs to achieve a superhuman leap, enabling players to surprise enemies, access otherwise unreachable areas, and navigate the game world with greater efficiency.

Macro Execution:

Activation: To activate the Super Jump macro, the player must press and hold the designated activation key (e.g., Spacebar) for a short duration (e.g., 0.5 seconds). This initial key press prepares the character for the super jump.

Charge: After the activation key is held for the required duration, the player must quickly release and re-press the activation key. This action initiates the charging phase, indicated by a visual cue (e.g., character crouching or glowing).

Release: Once the charge is complete (typically signaled by a visual or audio cue), the player releases the activation key. This triggers the super jump, launching the character into the air with incredible force and height.

Directional Control: During the jump, the player can control the direction of the jump by using the movement keys (e.g., W, A, S, D), allowing for mid-air adjustments and precise landings.

Cooldown: To prevent spamming and maintain game balance, the Super Jump macro has a cooldown period between uses, during which the player cannot perform another super jump.</Description>
    <Comment>its great </Comment>
    <GUIOption>
      <RepeatType>0</RepeatType>
    </GUIOption>
